<title>BELGIUM: EU Commission to investigate beef dumping.</title>
<headline>EU Commission to investigate beef dumping.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A complaint by South Africa that European Union beef traders are dumping beef on their market is to be investigated by the European Commission, an EU member state official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Farm ministers were told on Wednesday that exports to South Africa had increased to 41,000 tonnes in 1995 from 3,500 tonnes in 1992 and that the market was being disrupted.</p>
<p>&quot;The Union has been criticised by the South African government and the German public has been critical of export subsidies being used to support his trade,&quot; the German official said.</p>
<p>The issue was raised by Germany at the farm Council and the Commission promised to investigate, the official added.</p>
